        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/PlayStation-Studios-logo.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>In spite of launching a handful of unquestionable winners this generation like <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/marvels-spider-man-2\">Marvel's Spider-Man 2</a>, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/helldivers-2\">Helldivers 2</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/ghost-of-yotei\">Ghost of Y&omacr;tei</a>, PlayStation Studios has struggled with making the PS5's tenure super exciting. Of course, development cycles going totally off the rails and first-party exclusives (outside of Nintendo) becoming less and less important overall are part of the problem, but a failed live-service push can't be over-looked, either.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-studios-ramp-up-hiring-following-closures-and-cancellations\">Read more</a></p>",
